      "writtenOn": "2022-02-02T21:47:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could use a Kconfig symbol for general AP power sequence support.\n\nmenuconfig AP_PWRSEQ\n\n\nif AP_PWRSEQ\n\n# all the kconfigs\n\nendif\n\n\nYou should also consistently use \"pwrseq\" or \"power_seq\".  I think I prefer the shorter \"pwrseq\".",
      "revId": "d9178582d3242d155cb8bae1e9d9f08b1df4bdd3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8ce1123_6d84861e",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/Kconfig",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 6,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-02T21:47:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I recommend making this a \"helper\" symbol - a config that cannot be enabled directly by the user.\nhttps://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/guides/build/kconfig/tips.html#id8\n\nThis would look like (note the empty prompt on the bool property)\n\nconfig X86_NON_DSX_POWER_SEQ\n    bool \n    help\n       This option...\n       \nconfig X86_NON_DSX_POWER_SEQ_ADL\n    bool \"x86 non DSx on ADL\"\n    depends on AP_X86_INTEL_ADL\n    select X86_NON_DSX_POWER_SEQ\n    help\n        This adds...",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "d9178582d3242d155cb8bae1e9d9f08b1df4bdd3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
